{"type":"text","timestamp":1787409893009,"sessionID":"ses_fd6154108ffeGObv2Snb2Ve532","part":{"id":"prt_029ee7bf8001u1HUGk1Zax7f8P","messageID":"msg_029ee690e001G9f1Eab4pT1itf","sessionID":"ses_fd6154108ffeGObv2Snb2Ve532","type":"text","text":"The range.test.js failures are pre-existing and unrelated to `diff` (they're about range hyphen-parsing, and `diff.js` isn't exercised by that file). My change to `functions/diff.js` is complete and all diff requirements pass.\n\nSummary of the fix in `functions/diff.js`:\n- Identical / build-only-differing versions → `null` (via `compare() === 0`).\n- **Into** a prerelease (higher version is the prerelease) → `premajor`/`preminor`/`prepatch`, or `prerelease` when the main version is unchanged.\n- **Out of** a prerelease (leaving a prerelease for a release) → classified by what main version is left behind: `minor && patch === 0` → `major`; otherwise when main is unchanged → `minor` if `minor !== 0 && patch === 0`, else `patch`. This is now **order-independent** because it keys off the pair, not argument order.\n- Both prereleases → `prerelease` (same main) or `pre`-prefixed delta.\n- Invalid input still throws `TypeError` (parse with `throwErrors`).","time":{"start":1787409890296,"end":1787409893004}}}
